1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,107
Same one don of gold: buy at 750,000 won, sell right away for 640,000

2
00:00:05,127 --> 00:00:10,461
Where did 110,000 won go? It wasn't just the gold shop

3
00:00:10,481 --> 00:00:17,037
Korea Gold Exchange's Oct 26 board: two prices, a 110,000 won gap

4
00:00:17,057 --> 00:00:23,229
Culprit one is tax: nearly 70,000 is VAT, 10% inside the buy price

5
00:00:23,249 --> 00:00:30,171
Culprit two: the shop's cut, about 40,000 won for remelting, remaking, moving and margin

6
00:00:30,191 --> 00:00:36,651
So to get from 640,000 back to 750,000, gold must rise 17% just to break even

7
00:00:36,671 --> 00:00:40,748
Add a crafting fee, like a baby ring, and the bar is higher

8
00:00:40,768 --> 00:00:46,199
A baby ring was a gift, never something to resell

9
00:00:46,219 --> 00:00:52,204
So how to lose less? It depends where you buy. The KRX gold market, via a brokerage account,

10
00:00:52,224 --> 00:00:57,561
trades in 1-gram units, with VAT only when you take delivery

11
00:00:57,581 --> 00:01:03,280
Up or down, gold shops and dealers collect those 40,000 won on every trade

12
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:13,163
Korea Gold Exchange's sales doubled to 7.7 trillion won, reports said: turnover, not profit, but a busy toll road

13
00:01:13,183 --> 00:01:20,119
If you ever sell: check purity and weight, compare 2-3 shops first

14
00:01:20,139 --> 00:01:26,602
Like and subscribe for more. Full video: profile link
